 "comments": [
  {
   "address": 6496,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "Receives the disk resource selector in A and saves it on the stack. Disables VIC raster interrupts and CIA 1 timer A, installs the loader-time vectors, exposes the KERNAL while keeping I/O active, clears the SID register range and colour RAM, then jumps to the TO-specific transition code at $8100."
  },
  {
   "address": 6569,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "Exchanges four pages and another $38 bytes at $1520 with the same span at $0393, using zero-page pointers $02/$04. A second exchange restores the original contents of those spans."
  },
  {
   "address": 6627,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "Pops the selector, doubles it, reads the corresponding destination word from $1A16 and the two-character name from $1A2A, then calls SETLFS and SETNAM for drive 8. Calls the low-RAM routine at $0393 before exchanging those bytes back."
  },
  {
   "address": 6678,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "Table of ten little-endian destination addresses. The loader copies the selected word into the immediate operands at $047F and $0483 before the low-memory call."
  },
  {
   "address": 6698,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "Consecutive two-byte names L0 through L5, IN, CM, MN and ED. The two bytes after these ten entries are a separate filename buffer, filled by the loader at $1A3E."
  },
  {
   "address": 33024,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "Peeks at the loader selector on the stack. For selector 6 it disables sprites, selects the display through $DD00 and $D018 and writes nine screen codes and their colour cells for GAME OVER before waiting; other selectors go straight to exchanging and loading."
  },
  {
   "address": 33089,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "Nine C64 screen codes for GAME OVER, copied to the screen by the TO routine at $811D."
  }
 ]
